  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A grant with sprk_expiresdate in the past confers no access: the record is absent from the caller's participation/grant set (FR-06 acceptance).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A grant with null expiry or future expiry confers access unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a contact whose ONLY grant on a record is expired is denied on that record (accessible-set + IsRecordAccessible seam).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The predicate is server-side ($filter), verified by inspecting the built query in tests.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Closed list of sprk_externalrecordaccess read paths documented; each carries the predicate or a written non-access-conferring rationale.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All unit tests pass; build green; publish size reported in PR and ≤60 MB.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-06; finding A-5; register D-1 (enforce branch chosen — UI input stays because it now works). No sweep job: expired rows remain in the table as inactive-by-read; Phase 5 attestation will see them.

COMPLETED 2026-08-23. A-5 closed; FR-06 enforced server-side on every conferring read path.

CLOSED READ-PATH LIST (acceptance criterion 5). Predicate ADDED: ExternalParticipationService
.QueryGrantSetAsync (per-contact), .QueryOrganizationGrantRowsAsync (org grants -- omitting it would let
any contact keep expired access via their firm), ExternalDataService.GetProjectContactIdsAsync (display
list whose contract says "active access"; a participant list disagreeing with enforcement is its own
hazard). Predicate DELIBERATELY OMITTED: ExternalGrantLifecycle.QueryActiveRowsAsync/RetrieveRowAsync
(grant upsert + revoke sweep) and ProjectClosureEndpoint.BuildActiveProjectGrantsFilter (cascade revoke)
-- filtering expiry there would make EXPIRED GRANTS UNREVOKABLE, skipping exactly the rows an operator is
cleaning up. AccessibleRecordSetService holds no query of its own and inherits the fix.

THE PREDICATE: (sprk_expiresdate eq null or sprk_expiresdate ge {today:yyyy-MM-dd})

DEVIATION FROM THIS TASK'S PRESCRIBED STEP 2, on new evidence. Step 2 specifies
"(sprk_expiresdate eq null or sprk_expiresdate gt {utcNow})". Live Dataverse metadata shows
sprk_expiresdate is DATE ONLY, which the task author did not know. (a) {utcNow} as a timestamp against a
Date Only column risks a 400 -- and a 400 on this query returns an EMPTY grant set, i.e. a silent total
access outage rather than a visible error; the literal must be a bare yyyy-MM-dd. (b) gt kills a grant at
00:00 ON its own expiry date, silently shortening every dated grant in the system by one day; "access
until 30 June" means 30 June works. ge still satisfies FR-06, whose acceptance is an expiry IN THE PAST.
Pinned by ExpiryPredicate_OnTheExpiryDateItself_StillConfersAccess.

THE eq null BRANCH IS LOAD-BEARING: OData "ge" excludes nulls and most grants have no expiry, so without
it the predicate would revoke every open-ended grant -- an outage, not an expiry bug.

ESCALATION TRIGGERS -- both evaluated, NEITHER fired. (1) Live logical name verified via Dataverse
metadata; sprk_expiresdate is correct. The TYPE differed from the assumption and is handled above.
(2) All three paths build OData $filter strings directly -- no FetchXML composed elsewhere, nothing
filtered client-side.

TASK-001 OBLIGATION HONORED: BuildContactGrantFilter / BuildOrganizationGrantFilter / ExpiryPredicate /
GrantRowSelect extracted as pure internal static members BEFORE the predicate was added (task 001 could
not pin A-5 because the queries were inline immediately before _httpClient.SendAsync, and observing the
emitted $filter required a transport mock -- ban B1). No reflection (ban B8).

TESTS: tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/GrantExpiryCharacterizationTests.cs (11). NOTE the
test path named in this file (tests/unit/.../AccessControl/) is NOT a KEEP path and does not exist -- the
fifth POML in this project with a wrong test path. Perturbations: drop predicate 2/11 fail; drop eq null
1/11; ge->gt 1/11; ungroup org disjunction 1/11.

HONEST LIMIT: these assert the QUERY, not Dataverse's evaluation of it. End-to-end verification needs a
live tenant and is filed on task 034.

Full suite 10,726 passed / 0 failed; ArchTests 36/36; Core 45/45; publish 43.69 MB compressed
(unchanged, ceiling 60); no vulnerable packages.

Rationale: notes/task-007-grant-expiry.md</notes>

